# The transcript tree is a byte contract (US-124): the gate compares raw bytes
# with no `trim` and no line-ending normalization, so a checkout that rewrote a
# `\n` into a `\r\n` would fail every scenario at once and blame the code. The
# recorded streams are pinned with the transcripts they produce, because a `\r`
# in an input travels into the output.
crates/agent-cli/tests/transcripts/** -text
crates/agent-cli/tests/fixtures/*.sse -text
